  "worked_solution": "To compute the velocity vector, we need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \u27e8\\frac{1}{t+1},4\u27e9\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\u27e8\\int \\frac{1}{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 4\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t+1)+{C}_{1},4t+{C}_{2}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(1)=\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u206110,3\u27e9.$ Substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+1)+{C}_{1},4(1)+{C}_{2}\u27e9 \\\\ \u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u206110,3\u27e9 & =\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u20612+{C}_{1},4+{C}_{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u206110 & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20612+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}\u206110-\\operatorname{ln}\u20612 \\\\ {C}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\frac{10}{2}) \\\\ {C}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20615,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =4+{C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{2} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t+1)+\\operatorname{ln}\u20615,4t-1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061[5(t+1)],4t-1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(5t+5),4t-1\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
